WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:02.920
(lively music)

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:03.753
- [Narrator] China has been

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:05.650
on a global vaccine delivery drive

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.622
since the early days of the pandemic.

00:00:07.622 --> 00:00:09.610
(people clapping)

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.480
And Beijing gave that effort a boost

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.780
amid growing concerns over Omicron,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.373
a new coronarius variant

00:00:15.373 --> 00:00:18.196
that seems far more
transmissible than others.

00:00:18.196 --> 00:00:22.113
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.220
- [Narrator] The pledge
came after China said

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.500
it shipped 1.8 billion
vaccines to 120 countries.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.930
- I'm very grateful of this
huge donation to Africa.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.420
- China was very interested

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.310
in using its vaccines to advance a number

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.810
of geopolitical goals.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.850
- [Narrator] And the US
has its own goals too.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.910
- I think the US, based on its trials

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.660
is very confident in its vaccine.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.080
They feel like it's important for them

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.600
to be in league donating.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.150
- [Narrator] Less than a week

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.870
after Chinese president
Xi Jinping's pledge,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.390
President Biden also promised

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.940
to send nine million
extra vaccines to Africa.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:00:59.927
- I'm keeping the promise

00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:03.230
that America will become
the arsenal of vaccines.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.900
- [Narrator] China got out ahead of the US

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.910
in shipping it doses around the world

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.140
but the Biden administration
has said it's donated more.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.600
And now Omicron could challenge

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.373
both superpowers' vaccine
diplomacy efforts.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.910
But first, how was China
able to get a headstart?

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.580
As early as May of 2020,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.350
Beijing declared that it would
make its homegrown vaccines

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.520
a global public good.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.080
And it was able to make that promise

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.570
because it started
vaccinating its own population

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.920
with its doses a few months later.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.900
Then by September,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.580
China started shipping
its vaccines abroad.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.770
The US, on the other hand,

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.343
began sending doses nearly a year later.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.530
China was faster because
its vaccines were made

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.950
with traditional methods

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.930
and not with advanced genetic technology

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.060
like the first vaccines that
were approved in the US.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.630
This also meant Chinese doses

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.570
were easier to ship

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.220
since they didn't need to be stored

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.850
ultra-cold temperatures.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.100
Plus, state enterprises jumped in to help

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.800
with the vaccine supply chain,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.410
working with 19 countries to
manufacture doses locally.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.870
- Being the first is very important

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.950
because there's an element of stickiness.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.160
So in some ways, it
makes it more difficult

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.270
for the recipient countries

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.940
to buy vaccines from other
countries afterwards.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.440
- [Narrator] Bonny Lin is a senior fellow

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:17.310
at the Center for Strategic
and International Studies,

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.830
a bipartisan forum policy think tank.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.420
She's been tracking
China's vaccine diplomacy

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.790
and found that of the 1.1
billion doses Beijing agreed

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.330
to ship, 96% were designated as sales

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.290
and the rest as donations.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.130
China said its vaccines would be offered

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.080
at a fair and reasonable price,

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.860
and then says this
direct-to-consumer relationship

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.430
gives Beijing leverage.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.260
- One of the things that China does gain

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.601
is a bit more influence

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.470
over the recipient countries.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.680
And China was able to use its vaccines

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.510
to encourage countries to issue statements

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:53.930
in support of China.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.980
- [Narrator] For instance,
Paraguay said it was approached

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.710
by unofficial Chinese brokers

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.800
who offered to purchase vaccines
from China on its behalf

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.920
in return for breaking
diplomatic ties with Taiwan.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.120
It declined the offer and
China said the incident

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.878
was malicious disinformation.

00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:09.730
(people clapping)

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.460
Countries in the Indo-Pacific region

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.621
have also been receiving Chinese doses

00:03:13.621 --> 00:03:16.790
and that's grabbed the attention
of another vaccine donor.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.230
- The United States
has focused quite a bit

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.440
of our efforts in trying
to provide vaccines

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.370
in that region in order to push back

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.160
against whatever influence China may have.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.400
- [Narrator] And the US has been trying

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.700
to lead by donating its
vaccines to poorer countries.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.260
And a majority of them are
from Pfizer and BioNTech,

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.590
and Moderna, which have
high efficacy rates

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.940
against the original variant of the virus.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.653
Compare that with China's vaccines.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.990
A study by Bahrain and Columbia University

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.750
also found that the death
rate for Sinopharm recipients

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.380
was three times higher than
those inoculated with Pfizer.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.590
Lin says the efficacy of Chinese vaccines

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.010
may have dented Beijing's
efforts to gain influence.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.080
- A number of countries
are much more cautious now

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.210
about taking Chinese vaccines,

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:03.130
and there're increasing questions

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.710
of why does China need

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.930
to have such a stringent zero-tolerance,

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:10.080
and many suspect it's because of its lack

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.073
of confidence in its own vaccines.

00:04:14.165 --> 00:04:15.660
- [Narrator] And now the emergence

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.320
of a new fast-spreading variant

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.940
has triggered a wave
of fresh restrictions.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.420
And Omicron is forcing leaders

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.330
to speed up vaccination
drives around the world.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.010
- Individuals I talk with
in the administration

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.190
are really concerned.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:28.910
Unless we get everyone vaccinated,

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.490
new variants will crop up.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.450
I also think there's been
a fair amount of pressure

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.463
on the administration to do more,

00:04:34.463 --> 00:04:38.270
to help with donation
and to help lead a lot

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.470
of the world efforts.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:40.303
- [Narrator] In about a week

00:04:40.303 --> 00:04:41.860
of Omicron being declared a variant

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.870
of concern by the WHO,

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:47.220
but the US and China made
pledges to ship more vaccines.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.700
- It's about what can
be done collaboratively

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.990
to try and bring the pandemic to heel?

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.040
And I think just from
what we've seen so far,

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.290
especially with this new variant,

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.060
that just becomes more urgent.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.670
- [Narrator] But those efforts also rely

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.350
on how current vaccines respond to Omicron

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.520
and when boosters could be
available to poorer countries.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.040
A Hong Kong University
study found two doses

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.220
of the Sinopharm vaccine do
not produce enough antibodies

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.220
to fight against a new variant.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.110
Meanwhile, Pfizer and BioNTech said

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.570
that initial lab tests showed

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.360
that two doses were
significantly less efficacious

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.980
at blocking infection

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.400
but a third dose neutralized Omicron.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.870
And Moderna said a third dose

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.890
of its vaccine increased immune responses

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.860
against the new variant.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.640
So while both superpowers compete

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.080
to lead with vaccines,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.990
it may ultimately come down
to how effective the doses are

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.023
against new emerging variants.

